  "body": "What changed: WCS Turn X/Y/Z buttons rotate about the setup's current axes. The page now names the setup axes.\n\nCause: The quarter turn was left-composed with the orientation, so it acted in the world frame. Right composition applies it in the setup frame.\n\nTests: `quarter_turns_follow_each_oblique_setup_axis_in_both_directions` pins all three axes and both signs on an oblique setup and preserves the origin. The earlier run recorded that this pin failed before the fix. Its mutation restoring the old composition failed; restoring the fix passed. The publication run rechecked the pin, quick gate, and camcraft-ui all-targets clippy.\n\nGoldens moved: None. No NC or CL goldens changed.\n\nNot exercised: Interactive GUI clicks and physical machining.\n\nOverlaps: Changes are limited to the WCS page, its tests, and the issue decision file. No stacked dependency. Fork synced at v0.19.0; this branch also includes current upstream/main.\n\nChangelog: WCS quarter turns now rotate about the setup's own axes.\n\nFixes #1495\n\n\n## Screenshots\n\nRendered off-screen with the UI test harness in the default dark theme at 1280×800. Before is upstream/main; After is this PR's head. The ribbon/browser styling also differs because upstream/main has newer unrelated UI changes.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1684/before-wcs.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1684/after-wcs.png) |\n\nThe same oblique setup starts at roll 23°, pitch −31°, yaw 47°; look at the quarter-turn hint changing from world axes to setup axes.\n\n| Before | After |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1684/before-turn-x.png) | ![after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/1684/after-turn-x.png) |\n\nAfter the same Turn X+ click, compare the WCS triad and orientation fields: this PR gives roll 113°, pitch −31°, yaw 47°, preserving the setup-axis turn.\n",
